---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProcessSteps from '../components/ProcessSteps.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../config/schema';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const description =
	'Meridian Integrations designs the technology behind Colorado homes and businesses — websites, networks, cameras, EV charging, and automation you can own.';
const path = Astro.url.pathname;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description={description}
	path={path}
	extraSchema={[breadcrumbNode([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path }])]}
>
	<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
		<div class="wrap">
			<ol>
				<li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
				<li><span aria-current="page">About</span></li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</nav>

	<header class="page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">The practice</p>
			<h1>The infrastructure behind a modern property.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Meridian Integrations is a Colorado technology practice for homes, businesses, and the buildings that sit
				beside them. Websites, networks, cameras, EV charging, and automation are one body of work.
			</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="section" aria-labelledby="who-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="who-heading">Competence, kept quiet.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					The company people call when they want the technology done properly is rarely the one with the loudest
					website. The work is planning and installing systems that disappear into daily use: a site that loads and
					belongs to the business, a network that reaches the rooms, cameras that keep their footage, a charger that
					respects the panel, lighting that recalls a scene.
				</p>
				<p>
					{site.tagline} The supporting line is digital, network, energy, and automation — security included with
					the network, because cameras and segmentation are not a separate hobby.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-cream" aria-labelledby="own-heading">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2 id="own-heading">Designed around ownership.</h2>
			<ul class="index-list">
				<li>
					<strong>Websites</strong>
					<p>Source code you can hold, history you can roll back, and no page-builder lease as the price of editing a page.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Networks</strong>
					<p>Documented UniFi architecture on equipment the property controls.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Security</strong>
					<p>Local recording options and remote viewing that is intentional.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Automation</strong>
					<p>Lutron lighting and shades, with Josh.ai only when it earns a place in the design.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Charging</strong>
					<p>Electrical capacity understood before a charger is promised a circuit it cannot have.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<aside class="note">
				<p>
					Equipment is chosen from makers including Ubiquiti UniFi, Lutron, Josh.ai, GitHub, and Cloudflare. Working
					with those technologies is not the same thing as an authorized dealership, a partnership, or a
					manufacturer certification. None of those are claimed here.
				</p>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2 id="process-heading">How a project moves.</h2>
			<ProcessSteps />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-cream" aria-labelledby="not-heading">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="not-heading">What this is not.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Not a generic web agency, a computer-repair counter, a handyman list, or a catalog of smart-home gadgets.
					Not a call center. Projects start with the property or the business and end with something documented.
				</p>
				<p>
					There is no invented headcount, founding year, or stack of testimonials on this site. Trust is the
					clarity of the recommendation, not a badge that was not earned in public.
				</p>
				<p>
					The service area is the <a href="/service-area/">Denver Metro and surrounding Colorado communities</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<CTA title="Discuss your project." label="Request a Consultation" href="/contact/" />
</BaseLayout>
